IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ma-s03-exclusion`

-- Tests for ma-s03-exclusion.l4.  Every expected value is written from the text of s 3 before the run:
-- "If a contract contains a term which would exclude or restrict (a) any liability to which a party to a contract may be
-- subject by reason of any misrepresentation made by him before the contract was made; or (b) any remedy available to another
-- party to the contract by reason of such a misrepresentation, that term shall be of no effect except in so far as it satisfies the
-- requirement of reasonableness as stated in section 11(1) of the Unfair Contract Terms Act 1977, and it is for those claiming that
-- the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does."

§ `Tests -- s 3(a) and (b)`

#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3(a) or (b) the contract contains a term of a kind that section 3 reaches` NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 3, "that term shall be of no effect"`

-- Arguments: (a) liability excluded or restricted; (b) remedy excluded or restricted; the term satisfies the requirement of reasonableness.
-- A term within (a), not reasonable: of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A term within (b), not reasonable: of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Within both, not reasonable: of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "except in so far as it satisfies the requirement of reasonableness": the exception is met, so it is not of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Neither (a) nor (b): the "if" condition fails; section 3 does not touch the term, whatever its reasonableness.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Reasonableness not given: NOTHING, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Which limb is not given: either limb known true settles that the section reaches the term.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST TRUE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Whether the section reaches the term is not decided: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` (JUST FALSE) NOTHING (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests -- s 3, "it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does"`

-- Arguments: (a); (b); the party asked about is one of those claiming that the term satisfies the requirement.
#ASSERT `s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A party who makes no such claim: the text names only those claiming, so it is not covered, NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The section does not reach the term: no burden arises.
#ASSERT `s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Facts not given: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Tests -- s 3, the burden read with the bar: "it is for those claiming that the term satisfies that requirement to show that it does"`

-- Arguments: (a); (b); those claiming that the term satisfies the requirement have shown that it does.
-- A term within (a), and those claiming it is reasonable have NOT shown that it is: the requirement is not met, so the term is of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- A term within (b), not shown: of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Within both, not shown: of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Shown: the exception is met, so the term is not of no effect.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Whether it has been shown is not given: NOTHING, never FALSE.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- Neither (a) nor (b): section 3 does not reach the term, shown or not.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) NOTHING EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Which limb is not given: either limb known true settles that the section reaches the term.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` NOTHING (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Whether the section reaches the term is not decided: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` NOTHING (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 3 the term is of no effect, it being for those claiming that it satisfies the requirement to show that it does` NOTHING NOTHING NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
